# Unity compile status (agent gate)

Grid Dungeon uses [`com.miraluna.editor-agent-compile`](../../com.miraluna.editor-agent-compile) for structured compile checks while the Editor stays open.

Authority: [Tools/README.md](../../Tools/README.md), package [README.md](../../com.miraluna.editor-agent-compile/README.md).

## When to run (agents)

After any handoff-touching **`.cs`** change when the Unity Editor **may be open** on `griddungeon-game`:

```powershell
cd <griddungeon-game>
.\Tools\request-compile-status.ps1
```

- Exit **0** required before claiming compile-clean or closing a C# ticket.
- Exit **1** — fix reported `CS####` lines; re-run until green.
- Exit **2** — timeout; confirm Editor is open on this project and package resolved.
- Exit **3** — Editor did not claim request; open project in Unity.

Do **not** run `Tools/ci-compile.ps1` while the Editor has this project open (project lock). See `unity-no-cli-tests-while-editor-open.mdc`.

## Fallbacks

| Situation | Command |
|-----------|---------|
| Read last JSON without triggering compile | `.\Tools\read-compile-status.ps1` |
| Package/JSON unavailable | `.\Tools\read-unity-editor-log.ps1` |
| Editor closed | `.\Tools\ci-compile.ps1` |

## Output

Structured errors live in `Logs/last-compile.json` (gitignored): `file`, `line`, `column`, `message`.

Unity menu equivalent: **Tools → Miraluna → Request Compile Status**.

## Other projects

Install the same UPM package via `manifest.json`, copy/wrap `Tools/*.ps1`, add an equivalent cursor rule in that repo.
